---
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Specimen from "../components/Specimen.astro";
import { sections } from "../data";
const roles = ["display", "h1", "h2", "h3", "lead", "body", "small", "label", "caption"];
---
<Section {...sections.type}>
  <p slot="summary">Native elements keep their meaning. A role class selects an intentional visual treatment. Static, fluid, and mixed recipes share these selectors.</p>
  <Specimen id="headings" title="Roles">
    <div class="sg-type-list">
      {roles.map((role) => <article class="sg-type-row"><code>.{role}</code><p class={role}>{role}</p></article>)}
    </div>
    <p>Native h1–h3 match their roles; h4–h6 use h3. Native small, label, and figcaption use their own roles.</p>
  </Specimen>
  <Specimen id="long-content" title="Long content">
    <article class="s" data-fixture="type-long-content">
      <h4 data-fixture="type-semantic-heading">Semantic headings retain a readable measure when a long sentence needs more than one line to communicate its complete meaning.</h4>
      <h4 class="h1" data-fixture="type-visual-override">A semantic heading can use an explicit visual role without changing its document level.</h4>
      <p class="lead" data-fixture="type-large-text">Lead text establishes the subject and keeps its own readable measure.</p>
      <p class="body" data-fixture="type-body-text">Body text stays readable when the content reveals its measure and ordinary wrapping.</p>
      <p class="small" data-fixture="type-small-text">Supporting text uses a role-owned measure.</p>
      <ul data-fixture="type-inheritance"><li data-fixture="type-inherited-item">Lists inherit body type.</li></ul>
    </article>
  </Specimen>
  <Specimen id="line-clamp" title="Line clamp">
    <p l="2" data-fixture="type-clamp">A supporting paragraph can stop after two lines when the heading already carries the meaning and the extra sentences would push the following action out of the first screen.</p>
    <p class="small"><code>l="2"</code> keeps the full text in the DOM.</p>
  </Specimen>
  <Specimen id="elements" title="Native text and fonts">
    <p><strong>Strong</strong> and <b>bold</b> use ordinary font-weight, preserving custom axes. <em>Emphasis</em> keeps native meaning.</p>
    <p><small>Small print</small> · <mark>Marked text</mark> · <code>const role = "body"</code></p>
    <blockquote><p>A quotation remains a quotation, not an alias for a lead.</p></blockquote>
    <p>Bundled sans supports weight and optical size; mono supports weight. Project quote/code treatments remain extensions.</p>
  </Specimen>
</Section>
